ock. Whenever I have leftover sauces I try to find the next thing they can go into because they are so convenient and often provide a greater flavor profile than mixing fresh ingredients together because the flavors had time to bloom and get happy.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"24voj","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"4pfna","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"5mcni","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_34327d214d7144d091b40d0e2ba8ac73~mv2.jpg"},"width":1500,"height":1125},"altText":"Pan-Seared Flank Steak"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"7d0o6","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"d3qo9","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"After marinating for at least 2 hours or overnight, bring the steak to room temperature then pan sear over medium high heat for 6 minutes. Turn the steak over and sear for 5-6 more minutes.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"9pgt8","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"a2guk","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Now use tongs or another utensil to push gently on the top of the steak to see how firm it feels. Hold your hand out palm up and push on the pad of